"modebar-btn" data-title="Zoom in" data-attr="zoom" data-val="in" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 875 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m1 787l0-875 875 0 0 875-875 0z m687-500l-187 0 0-187-125 0 0 187-188 0 0 125 188 0 0 187 125 0 0-187 187 0 0-125z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Zoom out" data-attr="zoom" data-val="out" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 875 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m0 788l0-876 875 0 0 876-875 0z m688-500l-500 0 0 125 500 0 0-125z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Autoscale" data-attr="zoom" data-val="auto" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m250 850l-187 0-63 0 0-62 0-188 63 0 0 188 187 0 0 62z m688 0l-188 0 0-62 188 0 0-188 62 0 0 188 0 62-62 0z m-875-938l0 188-63 0 0-188 0-62 63 0 187 0 0 62-187 0z m875 188l0-188-188 0 0-62 188 0 62 0 0 62 0 188-62 0z m-125 188l-1 0-93-94-156 156 156 156 92-93 2 0 0 250-250 0 0-2 93-92-156-156-156 156 94 92 0 2-250 0 0-250 0 0 93 93 157-156-157-156-93 94 0 0 0-250 250 0 0 0-94 93 156 157 156-157-93-93 0 0 250 0 0 250z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a></div><div class="modebar-group"><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Toggle Spike Lines" data-attr="_cartesianSpikesEnabled" data-val="on" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="M512 409c0-57-46-104-103-104-57 0-104 47-104 104 0 57 47 103 104 103 57 0 103-46 103-103z m-327-39l92 0 0 92-92 0z m-185 0l92 0 0 92-92 0z m370-186l92 0 0 93-92 0z m0-184l92 0 0 92-92 0z" transform="matrix(1.5 0 0 -1.5 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Show closest data on hover" data-attr="hovermode" data-val="closest" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="ne"><svg viewBox="0 0 1500 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m375 725l0 0-375-375 375-374 0-1 1125 0 0 750-1125 0z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn active" data-title="Compare data on hover" data-attr="hovermode" data-val="x" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="ne"><svg viewBox="0 0 1125 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m187 786l0 2-187-188 188-187 0 0 937 0 0 373-938 0z m0-499l0 1-187-188 188-188 0 0 937 0 0 376-938-1z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a></div><div class="modebar-group"><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Save plot as PNG" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m500 450c-83 0-150-67-150-150 0-83 67-150 150-150 83 0 150 67 150 150 0 83-67 150-150 150z m400 150h-120c-16 0-34 13-39 29l-31 93c-6 15-23 28-40 28h-340c-16 0-34-13-39-28l-31-94c-6-15-23-28-40-28h-120c-55 0-100-45-100-100v-450c0-55 45-100 100-100h800c55 0 100 45 100 100v450c0 55-45 100-100 100z m-400-550c-138 0-250 112-250 250 0 138 112 250 250 250 138 0 250-112 250-250 0-138-112-250-250-250z m365 380c-19 0-35-16-35-35 0-19 16-35 35-35 19 0 35 16 35 35 0 19-16 35-35 35z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Open in dialog (edit layout)" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="M786 296v-267q0-15-11-26t-25-10h-214v214h-143v-214h-214q-15 0-25 10t-11 26v267q0 1 0 2t0 2l321 264 321-264q1-1 1-4z m124 39l-34-41q-5-5-12-6h-2q-7 0-12 3l-386 322-386-322q-7-4-13-4-7 2-12 7l-35 41q-4 5-3 13t6 12l401 334q18 15 42 15t43-15l136-114v109q0 8 5 13t13 5h107q8 0 13-5t5-13v-227l122-102q5-5 6-12t-4-13z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a></div></div></div><svg class="main-svg" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" width="694" height="377.33333333333337"><g class="hoverlayer"></g></svg></div></div></div></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(640,20)" x="640" y="20" title="codeHTML" width="560" height="773" class="codeHTML" name="codeHTML" rot="0"><foreignObject x="0" y="0" width="560" height="773" style="width: 560px; height: 773px;"><div name="htmlCode" style="zoom: 0.56; height: 1380.36px; width: 1000px;" code="&lt;div class=&quot;ch&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Tunnel Diode Oscillator with a Bias Network&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;ch-card&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Circuit Components&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The circuit is drawn in three blocks, as in the classical textbook figure:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bias circuit:&lt;/strong&gt; battery &lt;em&gt;Vb&lt;/em&gt; = 1.5 V, switch &lt;em&gt;SW&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;em&gt;SwitchSPST&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;state&lt;/em&gt; = 1: closed), series resistor &lt;em&gt;R1&lt;/em&gt; = 60 &amp;Omega; and shunt resistor &lt;em&gt;Rs&lt;/em&gt; = 12 &amp;Omega;. They form a voltage divider that sets the operating point of the diode&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tunnel diode (TD):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;TunnelDiode&lt;/em&gt;, I&lt;sub&gt;p&lt;/sub&gt; = 5 mA at V&lt;sub&gt;p&lt;/sub&gt; = 0.1 V. The anode is on the node &lt;em&gt;A&lt;/em&gt; (the divider) and the cathode on the node &lt;em&gt;T&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tank circuit:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Cr&lt;/em&gt; = 100 pF and &lt;em&gt;Lr&lt;/em&gt; = 1 &amp;micro;H in parallel, from &lt;em&gt;T&lt;/em&gt; to ground&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Load:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;RL&lt;/em&gt; = 1 k&amp;Omega; from &lt;em&gt;T&lt;/em&gt; to ground&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Principle&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Between its peak (0.10 V, 5.00 mA) and its valley (0.43 V, 1.15 mA) the tunnel diode has a &lt;strong&gt;negative resistance&lt;/strong&gt;: the current decreases when the voltage increases. The steepest slope is &amp;minus;18.2 mS, that is &amp;minus;55 &amp;Omega;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;ch-grid&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-col blue&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;DC: the operating point&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The divider is equivalent to a source $V_{th} = V_b \dfrac{R_s}{R_1 + R_s}$ in series with $R_{th} = R_1 \parallel R_s$&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;$V_{th} = 1.5 \times 12 / 72 = \mathbf{0.25\ V}$ and $R_{th} = \mathbf{10\ \Omega}$&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lr is a short circuit for DC, so the whole $V_{th}$ is applied to the diode through $R_{th}$: it is biased in the middle of the negative-resistance region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For a stable bias point: $R_{th} &lt; |r_{neg}| \approx 55\ \Omega$&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-col red&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;AC: the oscillation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For the high frequencies the battery and the divider are a low impedance: the node &lt;em&gt;A&lt;/em&gt; is an AC ground, in series with $R_{th}$&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;So the diode, with a net negative resistance $-(|r| - R_{th})$, is connected across the tank Cr&amp;#8214;Lr and the load RL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The oscillation starts if this negative resistance compensates the losses of the tank and of the load&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lr blocks the DC component: the load voltage oscillates around &lt;strong&gt;0 V&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Results of the Simulation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-formula&quot;&gt;
$f_{sim} \approx \mathbf{12.2\ MHz}$ &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; $V_T:\ -0.32\ V \rightarrow +0.24\ V$ &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; $V_A:\ 0.20\ V \rightarrow 0.25\ V$
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The frequency of the oscillation is &lt;strong&gt;12.20 MHz&lt;/strong&gt;, the same as the oscillator of the demo &lt;em&gt;Tunnel Diode Oscillator&lt;/em&gt;, which has the same diode, L and C&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The voltage on the load &lt;em&gt;T&lt;/em&gt; goes from &lt;strong&gt;&amp;minus;0.319 V to +0.243 V&lt;/strong&gt; and its mean value is 2.5 mV: the signal is centred on zero, as in the figure. The first swing already appears after about 3 ns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The anode node &lt;em&gt;A&lt;/em&gt; only has a ripple, between &lt;strong&gt;0.199 V and 0.246 V&lt;/strong&gt; (the divider holds it near 0.25 V)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current of the coil: between &amp;minus;1.2 mA and +6.2 mA. Current of the diode: between 0.4 mA and 5.1 mA (it stays inside the range of the I(V) curve)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Reading the Plot&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;T&lt;/strong&gt;: the output of the oscillator, on the load, centred on 0 V&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A&lt;/strong&gt;: the node between the divider and the diode, nearly constant: this is the bias&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;How to Run It&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-card&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0;&quot;&gt;Press &lt;strong&gt;Start Analysis&lt;/strong&gt; in the analysis block (Time Domain, 0 to 2 &amp;micro;s, step 0.2 ns; options &lt;em&gt;uic&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;adaptive&lt;/em&gt; and &lt;em&gt;order 2&lt;/em&gt;). The switch is closed (&lt;em&gt;state&lt;/em&gt; = 1) at the beginning: the battery is connected at t = 0, which starts the oscillation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Things to Try&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-card&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the &lt;em&gt;state&lt;/em&gt; of SW to 0: the switch is open, nothing is powered and both T and A stay at 0 V&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set Vb to 3 V: the bias is above the valley and A settles to 0.485 V: no oscillation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change R1 to 30 &amp;Omega;: the bias is 0.43 V, at the edge of the negative-resistance region. The oscillation is weak: T between &amp;minus;0.058 V and +0.058 V&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change R1 to 300 &amp;Omega; and Rs to 60 &amp;Omega; (the same V&lt;sub&gt;th&lt;/sub&gt; = 0.25 V but R&lt;sub&gt;th&lt;/sub&gt; = 50 &amp;Omega;, almost the whole negative resistance): the bias is not stable, A settles to 0.048 V and the oscillation does not start&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce RL to 100 &amp;Omega;: the load takes more of the power; T goes from &amp;minus;0.21 V to +0.17 V and the frequency becomes 13.6 MHz&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increase Cr to 400 pF: 7.2 MHz. Increase Lr to 4 &amp;micro;H: 4.6 MHz. The frequency follows the tank, the amplitude stays almost the same&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
"> 
    <!-- Parent container that responds to mouse movement -->
    <div class="chtool"> 
        
        <!-- tool bar-->
        <div class="ch-page-toolbar" style="zoom: 1.78571;">
